# Design System (DESIGN.md)

When building or editing UI, React components, or CSS in `apps/web`, **`apps/web/DESIGN.md` is required reading and the visual source of truth**.

## Where to look

1. **`apps/web/DESIGN.md`** — primary design spec (Notion warm-workspace system). **Always read this before any UI work.**
2. `DESIGN.md` at repo root — only if present; `apps/web/DESIGN.md` wins on conflict.

Also see `apps/web/AGENTS.md` for the web agent checklist.

## Required workflow

1. **Read** the full `apps/web/DESIGN.md` before writing components, pages, or styles.
2. **Treat it as source of truth** for colors, typography, spacing, layout, motion, and component patterns.
3. **Map tokens to code** — use values from `DESIGN.md` in `app/globals.css` (`:root`, `@theme`) and Tailwind utilities; do not invent conflicting palettes or type scales.
4. **Reuse documented patterns** — prefer components and class conventions named in `DESIGN.md` over one-off styles.
5. **On conflict** — `DESIGN.md` wins over generic frontend-design skill defaults and over default shadcn token looks when they disagree.
6. **Compose with `@repo/ui`** — use shared primitives, then align colors/radius/type to `DESIGN.md` tokens.

## Scope

Applies to: new pages, components, layout changes, `globals.css`, `@utility` / `@layer` blocks, and any Tailwind class composition for the web app.

Does **not** replace: `code-quality.mdc`, `web-structure.mdc`, React/Next.js performance skills, or accessibility checks from `web-design-guidelines`.
